# Hiding: a hidden thing stays faintly where it was and gives up its room; the rest closes up smoothly.
title "Done, step back"
schema graph
mark f1 tex tex="a + b = c"
mark f2 tex tex="c - b = a"
mark a box part label="first"
mark b box part label="second"
mark c box part label="third"
link ab arrow a -> b
link bc arrow b -> c
Say: "Three steps, two formulas."
hide f1
with hide b
Say: "The first formula and the middle step are done."
mark d box part label="next"
link cd arrow c -> d
Say: "And the flow goes on."
